That death was not by ledneh, but by Zadir.

Note that the Points is the maximum possible points one can get in
nethack, at least on a 32-bit machine--  2147483647 is the largest
number a signed int can hold.  If you go over that, you wrap around to
negative points.  And if you actually ascend, you get a point bonus, so
it is very hard to control exactly how many points you finish with
unless you die to finish the game.

Zadir wanted to set the highest score that is possible, so he farmed
one of the riders repeatedly, used leftover zorkmids to get exactly the
right number, and then committed suicide in what the IRC denizens of
#nethack decided was the most appropriate way, ensuring that nobody on
nethack.alt.org will ever have a higher score than him (at least until
new versions of the game lift the restriction, or maybe if nao moves to
a 64-bit platform).



